@startuml
title 1C - Discord: "/jardinero-code request:take over PR #FFF"\nThe ask hands the PR to the machine; from there it is the normal PR path

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User
participant "DiscordAdapter" as DA
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Store" as S
participant GitHub

User -> DA: /jardinero-code request:"take over PR #FFF"
DA -> DA: resolve identity + channel
return actor, repo
DA -> O: DiscordRequest{actor, channel, text}
O -> S: create RequestRouter instance
return rr_pending
O -> O: Router.resolve(request)  ' the subject is what picks the machine
return subject=pr:repo#FFF
O -> S: state
return rr_resolved

O -> O: PrMaintainer.OnPrToFollow{pr:repo#FFF, request}
O -> S: create PrMaintainer instance
return prm_pending
O -> DA: reply @user
return "on it"

note right of O
  The request machine ENDS here, and the PrMaintainer
  instance is the mandate: it lives in our storage and
  ends when the PR does.

  Tagging the agent on the PR skips Discord entirely and
  opens the same instance, see 2B.
end note

note right of O
  "resolve the conflicts of my own PR" is NOT a case:
  on our own PRs the PrMaintainer already does it on the
  next tick. Asking for it only means "do it now",
  which is priority, not a capability.
end note
@enduml
